<title>LITHUANIA: FOREIGN INVESTORS TAKE BIG STAKE IN SANITAS.</title>
<headline>FOREIGN INVESTORS TAKE BIG STAKE IN SANITAS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors bought around 50 percent of the shares in Lithuanian pharmaceutical producer Sanitas on Thursday in a block deal worth 33.5 million litas, Suprema brokerage house said.  </p>
<p>&quot;Eight foreign funds and private persons bought the shares,&quot; Arvydas Jacikevicius, a dealer with Suprema, told Reuters. </p>
<p>He said that Suprema registered the deal but declined to say which funds or persons were involved.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
